Polish findings from the live smoke test

- the run row gets its selected count and sources right after
  selection, so the monitor no longer shows 0/0 for a running run;
- counts on cards use proper Russian plural forms;
- the force-run block is left-aligned on narrow screens;
- README: results of the end-to-end check on live data and the
  trade-off of strict let's play title matching.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Protect the force-run button and lock down the web pages

Force run stays open for reviewers but cannot be abused:
- 409 while a run is active (in-process lock plus the DB lease);
- a cooldown of MANUAL_RUN_COOLDOWN_SECONDS (300) after the last run
  ends, answered with 429 and Retry-After, with a live countdown on
  the button;
- MANUAL_RUNS_PER_DAY (24) manual runs per day;
- POST /run and /api/run refuse cross-site requests (Sec-Fetch-Site /
  Origin) with 403;
- optional RUN_TOKEN (Bearer) f

Harden the run pipeline: migrations, retries, time limit, lease, safe updates

Database
- schema versioned with PRAGMA user_version; missing migrations are
  applied in one transaction at startup, old databases upgrade in
  place, a newer schema is refused;
- bounded connection pool (8) instead of one connection per thread;
- index on errors(day); old errors and processed rows are pruned;
- LIKE wildcards in search are escaped;
- run lease table so only one process can run the pipeline, and a ru

